From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:36:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: let Android Components seal places', logins' and cards'
 stores

PlacesHistoryStorage and PlacesBookmarksStorage, SyncableLoginsStorage
and AutofillCreditCardsAddressesStorage each take a database key: a
source of 32 bytes, asked for, and waited for, when the store first
opens its database. Without one, a store keeps its database in the
clear, as it always has. Places' connection is the process's own, so
every store of it must agree on whether it is sealed.

The stage 3 spike's patch 0003 (encriox W21), on the release
rather than on stage 1's changes to the logins' and autofill's stores.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
